--TEST--
A declared class written at any of `Core\Request`'s decoding members is asked for the qualifier its inline-shape sibling is asked for, at every one of them — `rule:security/derived-codec-qualifiers`, `rule:security/tainted-sources`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The class half of `an-unqualified-shape-at-a-request-decode-site-is-refused`,
// asked of all three members together: every `Core\Request` member that reads a
// parameter set reads a peer's octets, so which of them a call wrote cannot
// change the answer. Three classes rather than one, because the refusal is
// reported once per property however many sites reach it.
#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Body {
    public string $note;

    public function constructor(string $note) {
        $this->note = $note;
    }
}

#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Query {
    public string $q;

    public function constructor(string $q) {
        $this->q = $q;
    }
}

#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Form {
    public string $email;

    public function constructor(string $email) {
        $this->email = $email;
    }
}

// The accepted side of the bound, named beside the refused ones: `tainted` on
// the declaration is the whole of what the rule asks for, and no issue below is
// about this class.
#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Ok {
    public tainted string $term;

    public function constructor(tainted string $term) {
        $this->term = $term;
    }
}

var $body = Core\Request::jsonAs<Body>();
var $query = Core\Request::queryAs<Query>();
var $form = Core\Request::postAs<Form>();
var $ok = Core\Request::queryAs<Ok>();
echo $body->note, $query->q, $form->email, $ok->term, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0810]: `Body::$note` is declared `string`, and `Core\Request::jsonAs` answers a peer's octets
%A
error[E0810]: `Query::$q` is declared `string`, and `Core\Request::queryAs` answers a peer's octets
%A
error[E0810]: `Form::$email` is declared `string`, and `Core\Request::postAs` answers a peer's octets
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
